{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>על</b> The meaning is like one who guards his watch in the night watch, who is awake and opens his eyes to see, for the guards in the city divide the night into halves or into thirds and quarters." "<b>ואתיצבה על מצור</b> The meaning is doubled, to seek a path of prophecy as to why HaShem is silent." "<b>ומה אשיב על תוכחתי</b> To him who reproves me. The yod is a sign of the object acted upon, like ותוכחתי לבקרים, which is a noun of reproof that others direct at him. But ותוכחתי לא אביתם is not on this pattern, for the yod is a sign of the subject, that he is the one who reproves others."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:04.594304484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}